    <item>
      <title>Interactive Formal Verification Lab</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/playground/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 08 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/playground/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;I built these three tools to show how some of the ideas I work with actually behave. They are small, but they are real: the model checker explores every reachable state and checks your formula with the standard labelling algorithm, and the verifier computes weakest preconditions for whatever conditions you type in. Everything runs in your browser, so feel free to break things.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;link rel=&#34;stylesheet&#34; href=&#34;http://localhost:1313/css/fv_playground.css?v=e248c122&#34;&gt;

&lt;div class=&#34;fv-playground-wrapper not-prose&#34; id=&#34;fv-lab&#34;&gt;
  
  &lt;div class=&#34;fv-tabs&#34; role=&#34;tablist&#34;&gt;
    &lt;button type=&#34;button&#34; class=&#34;fv-tab-btn active&#34; role=&#34;tab&#34; aria-selected=&#34;true&#34; data-tab=&#34;sat-solver&#34;&gt;
      &lt;span class=&#34;tab-icon&#34;&gt;⚡&lt;/span&gt; DPLL SAT Solver
    &lt;/button&gt;
    &lt;button type=&#34;button&#34; class=&#34;fv-tab-btn&#34; role=&#34;tab&#34; aria-selected=&#34;false&#34; data-tab=&#34;model-checker&#34;&gt;
      &lt;span class=&#34;tab-icon&#34;&gt;🛡️&lt;/span&gt; CTL Model Checker
    &lt;/button&gt;
    &lt;button type=&#34;button&#34; class=&#34;fv-tab-btn&#34; role=&#34;tab&#34; aria-selected=&#34;false&#34; data-tab=&#34;hoare-logic&#34;&gt;
      &lt;span class=&#34;tab-icon&#34;&gt;🔍&lt;/span&gt; Hoare Logic Verifier
    &lt;/button&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;

  &lt;div class=&#34;fv-card&#34;&gt;

    
    &lt;div id=&#34;sat-solver&#34; class=&#34;fv-tab-content active&#34; role=&#34;tabpanel&#34;&gt;
      &lt;div class=&#34;fv-grid&#34;&gt;
        &lt;div class=&#34;fv-control-panel&#34;&gt;
          &lt;h3 class=&#34;panel-title&#34;&gt;Solver Controls&lt;/h3&gt;

          &lt;div class=&#34;form-group&#34;&gt;
            &lt;label for=&#34;sat-presets&#34;&gt;Formula&lt;/label&gt;
            &lt;select id=&#34;sat-presets&#34;&gt;
              &lt;option value=&#34;sat-simple&#34;&gt;Satisfiable: (A ∨ B) ∧ (¬A ∨ C) ∧ (¬B ∨ ¬C)&lt;/option&gt;
              &lt;option value=&#34;unsat-simple&#34;&gt;Unsatisfiable: all four clauses over A and B&lt;/option&gt;
              &lt;option value=&#34;chain&#34;&gt;Implication chain: refuted by propagation alone&lt;/option&gt;
              &lt;option value=&#34;php-3-2&#34;&gt;Pigeonhole: 3 pigeons, 2 holes (unsatisfiable)&lt;/option&gt;
              &lt;option value=&#34;custom&#34;&gt;Write your own CNF formula...&lt;/option&gt;
            &lt;/select&gt;
          &lt;/div&gt;

          &lt;div id=&#34;sat-custom-container&#34; class=&#34;form-group hidden&#34;&gt;
            &lt;label for=&#34;sat-custom-input&#34;&gt;Your formula in CNF&lt;/label&gt;
            &lt;input type=&#34;text&#34; id=&#34;sat-custom-input&#34; class=&#34;mono-input&#34; placeholder=&#34;(A | B) &amp; (~A | C) &amp; (~B | ~C)&#34; spellcheck=&#34;false&#34; autocomplete=&#34;off&#34;&gt;
            &lt;p class=&#34;hint-text&#34;&gt;Join clauses with &amp;amp; and literals with |. Negate with ~ or !. Up to 12 variables.&lt;/p&gt;
            &lt;div id=&#34;sat-parse-error&#34; class=&#34;error-text&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
          &lt;/div&gt;

          &lt;div class=&#34;control-buttons&#34;&gt;
            &lt;button type=&#34;button&#34; class=&#34;btn btn-primary&#34; id=&#34;btn-sat-solve&#34;&gt;Solve&lt;/button&gt;
            &lt;button type=&#34;button&#34; class=&#34;btn btn-secondary&#34; id=&#34;btn-sat-step&#34;&gt;Step&lt;/button&gt;
            &lt;button type=&#34;button&#34; class=&#34;btn btn-accent&#34; id=&#34;btn-sat-run&#34;&gt;Auto run&lt;/button&gt;
            &lt;button type=&#34;button&#34; class=&#34;btn btn-danger&#34; id=&#34;btn-sat-reset&#34;&gt;Reset&lt;/button&gt;
          &lt;/div&gt;

          &lt;div class=&#34;speed-control&#34;&gt;
            &lt;label for=&#34;sat-speed&#34;&gt;Auto run speed&lt;/label&gt;
            &lt;input type=&#34;range&#34; id=&#34;sat-speed&#34; min=&#34;100&#34; max=&#34;2000&#34; value=&#34;700&#34; step=&#34;100&#34;&gt;
            &lt;span class=&#34;speed-label&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
          &lt;/div&gt;

          &lt;div&gt;
            &lt;h4 class=&#34;sub-panel-title&#34;&gt;Assignment&lt;/h4&gt;
            &lt;div id=&#34;sat-assignments&#34; class=&#34;assignment-list&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
          &lt;/div&gt;

          &lt;div class=&#34;console-panel&#34;&gt;
            &lt;h4 class=&#34;sub-panel-title&#34;&gt;Solver log&lt;/h4&gt;
            &lt;div id=&#34;sat-logs&#34; class=&#34;console-log&#34; aria-live=&#34;polite&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
          &lt;/div&gt;
        &lt;/div&gt;

        &lt;div class=&#34;fv-visual-panel&#34;&gt;
          &lt;div class=&#34;panel-header-toolbar&#34;&gt;
            &lt;span class=&#34;panel-subtitle&#34;&gt;Clauses and search tree&lt;/span&gt;
            &lt;span id=&#34;sat-status&#34; class=&#34;badge badge-neutral&#34;&gt;IDLE&lt;/span&gt;
          &lt;/div&gt;

          &lt;div id=&#34;sat-stats&#34; class=&#34;stats-row&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

          &lt;div&gt;
            &lt;h4 class=&#34;sub-panel-title&#34;&gt;Clauses&lt;/h4&gt;
            &lt;div id=&#34;sat-formula-clauses&#34; class=&#34;clause-box&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
          &lt;/div&gt;

          &lt;div class=&#34;tree-container&#34;&gt;
            &lt;h4 class=&#34;sub-panel-title&#34;&gt;Search tree&lt;/h4&gt;
            &lt;div class=&#34;tree-canvas-wrapper&#34;&gt;
              &lt;svg id=&#34;sat-tree-svg&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 500 260&#34; preserveAspectRatio=&#34;xMidYMin meet&#34; role=&#34;img&#34; aria-label=&#34;DPLL search tree&#34;&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;
            &lt;/div&gt;
          &lt;/div&gt;

          &lt;div class=&#34;legend-box&#34;&gt;
            &lt;span class=&#34;legend-item&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;legend-shape legend-circle&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt; Decision&lt;/span&gt;
            &lt;span class=&#34;legend-item&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;legend-shape legend-diamond&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt; Forced by unit propagation&lt;/span&gt;
            &lt;span class=&#34;legend-item&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;legend-color conflict-color&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt; Conflict or dead end&lt;/span&gt;
            &lt;span class=&#34;legend-item&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;legend-color sat-color&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt; Satisfying path&lt;/span&gt;
          &lt;/div&gt;
        &lt;/div&gt;
      &lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;

    
    &lt;div id=&#34;model-checker&#34; class=&#34;fv-tab-content&#34; role=&#34;tabpanel&#34;&gt;
      &lt;div class=&#34;fv-grid&#34;&gt;
        &lt;div class=&#34;fv-control-panel&#34;&gt;
          &lt;h3 class=&#34;panel-title&#34;&gt;Model Checking&lt;/h3&gt;

          &lt;div class=&#34;form-group&#34;&gt;
            &lt;label for=&#34;mc-system&#34;&gt;System&lt;/label&gt;
            &lt;select id=&#34;mc-system&#34;&gt;
              &lt;option value=&#34;peterson&#34;&gt;Peterson&#39;s mutual exclusion&lt;/option&gt;
              &lt;option value=&#34;flags-only&#34;&gt;Flags only, no turn variable&lt;/option&gt;
              &lt;option value=&#34;naive-lock&#34;&gt;Naive lock: check first, then set&lt;/option&gt;
              &lt;option value=&#34;traffic&#34;&gt;Traffic light controller&lt;/option&gt;
            &lt;/select&gt;
            &lt;p id=&#34;mc-blurb&#34; class=&#34;hint-text&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
          &lt;/div&gt;

          &lt;div class=&#34;form-group&#34;&gt;
            &lt;label for=&#34;mc-property&#34;&gt;CTL property&lt;/label&gt;
            &lt;select id=&#34;mc-property&#34;&gt;&lt;/select&gt;
            &lt;input type=&#34;text&#34; id=&#34;mc-custom&#34; class=&#34;mono-input hidden&#34; spellcheck=&#34;false&#34; autocomplete=&#34;off&#34; aria-label=&#34;Custom CTL formula&#34;&gt;
            &lt;div id=&#34;mc-error&#34; class=&#34;error-text&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
            &lt;details class=&#34;syntax-help&#34;&gt;
              &lt;summary&gt;Formula syntax&lt;/summary&gt;
              &lt;p&gt;Atoms compare a variable with a value, like &lt;code&gt;pc0 = WAIT&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;turn != 1&lt;/code&gt;. Booleans can stand alone, like &lt;code&gt;flag0&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;deadlock&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
              &lt;p&gt;Connectives: &lt;code&gt;!&lt;/code&gt; &lt;code&gt;&amp;amp;&lt;/code&gt; &lt;code&gt;|&lt;/code&gt; &lt;code&gt;-&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;-&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;. Temporal operators: &lt;code&gt;AX EX AF EF AG EG&lt;/code&gt;, plus &lt;code&gt;A[p U q]&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;E[p U q]&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
            &lt;/details&gt;
          &lt;/div&gt;

          &lt;div class=&#34;control-buttons&#34;&gt;
            &lt;button type=&#34;button&#34; class=&#34;btn btn-primary&#34; id=&#34;btn-mc-verify&#34;&gt;Verify&lt;/button&gt;
            &lt;button type=&#34;button&#34; class=&#34;btn btn-secondary&#34; id=&#34;btn-mc-step&#34;&gt;Step&lt;/button&gt;
            &lt;button type=&#34;button&#34; class=&#34;btn btn-accent&#34; id=&#34;btn-mc-simulate&#34;&gt;Simulate&lt;/button&gt;
            &lt;button type=&#34;button&#34; class=&#34;btn btn-danger&#34; id=&#34;btn-mc-reset&#34;&gt;Reset&lt;/button&gt;
          &lt;/div&gt;

          &lt;div class=&#34;speed-control&#34;&gt;
            &lt;label for=&#34;mc-speed&#34;&gt;Simulation speed&lt;/label&gt;
            &lt;input type=&#34;range&#34; id=&#34;mc-speed&#34; min=&#34;100&#34; max=&#34;1500&#34; value=&#34;600&#34; step=&#34;100&#34;&gt;
            &lt;span class=&#34;speed-label&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
          &lt;/div&gt;

          &lt;div id=&#34;mc-verdict&#34; class=&#34;verdict-box hidden&#34; aria-live=&#34;polite&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

          &lt;div&gt;
            &lt;h4 class=&#34;sub-panel-title&#34;&gt;Current state: &lt;span id=&#34;mc-current-name&#34;&gt;S0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
            &lt;div id=&#34;mc-state-vars&#34; class=&#34;state-variables&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
            &lt;div id=&#34;mc-moves&#34; class=&#34;moves-list&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
          &lt;/div&gt;

          &lt;div class=&#34;console-panel&#34;&gt;
            &lt;h4 class=&#34;sub-panel-title&#34;&gt;Model checker log&lt;/h4&gt;
            &lt;div id=&#34;mc-logs&#34; class=&#34;console-log&#34; aria-live=&#34;polite&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
          &lt;/div&gt;
        &lt;/div&gt;

        &lt;div class=&#34;fv-visual-panel&#34;&gt;
          &lt;div class=&#34;panel-header-toolbar&#34;&gt;
            &lt;span class=&#34;panel-subtitle&#34;&gt;Reachable states&lt;/span&gt;
            &lt;span id=&#34;mc-status&#34; class=&#34;badge badge-neutral&#34;&gt;IDLE&lt;/span&gt;
          &lt;/div&gt;

          &lt;div class=&#34;kripke-container&#34;&gt;
            &lt;div class=&#34;graph-canvas-wrapper&#34;&gt;
              &lt;svg id=&#34;mc-graph-svg&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 550 450&#34; preserveAspectRatio=&#34;xMidYMid meet&#34; role=&#34;img&#34; aria-label=&#34;Kripke structure of the selected system&#34;&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;
            &lt;/div&gt;
            &lt;p class=&#34;hint-text&#34;&gt;Hover a state or an arrow for details. Click a state one step away from the current one to move there.&lt;/p&gt;
          &lt;/div&gt;

          &lt;div class=&#34;legend-box&#34;&gt;
            &lt;span class=&#34;legend-item&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;legend-color init-color&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt; Initial state&lt;/span&gt;
            &lt;span class=&#34;legend-item&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;legend-color sat-color&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt; Satisfies the formula&lt;/span&gt;
            &lt;span class=&#34;legend-item&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;legend-color current-color&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt; Current state&lt;/span&gt;
            &lt;span class=&#34;legend-item&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;legend-color counter-color&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt; Counterexample&lt;/span&gt;
            &lt;span class=&#34;legend-item&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;legend-color witness-color&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt; Witness&lt;/span&gt;
            &lt;span class=&#34;legend-item&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;legend-color deadlock-color&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt; Deadlock&lt;/span&gt;
          &lt;/div&gt;
        &lt;/div&gt;
      &lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;

    
    &lt;div id=&#34;hoare-logic&#34; class=&#34;fv-tab-content&#34; role=&#34;tabpanel&#34;&gt;
      &lt;div class=&#34;fv-grid&#34;&gt;
        &lt;div class=&#34;fv-control-panel&#34;&gt;
          &lt;h3 class=&#34;panel-title&#34;&gt;Program Verification&lt;/h3&gt;

          &lt;div class=&#34;form-group&#34;&gt;
            &lt;label for=&#34;hl-presets&#34;&gt;Program&lt;/label&gt;
            &lt;select id=&#34;hl-presets&#34;&gt;
              &lt;option value=&#34;abs&#34;&gt;Absolute value&lt;/option&gt;
              &lt;option value=&#34;swap&#34;&gt;Swap two variables (has a bug)&lt;/option&gt;
              &lt;option value=&#34;sum&#34;&gt;Sum of 1 to N (loop)&lt;/option&gt;
              &lt;option value=&#34;div&#34;&gt;Integer division (loop)&lt;/option&gt;
            &lt;/select&gt;
            &lt;p id=&#34;hl-hint&#34; class=&#34;hint-text&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
          &lt;/div&gt;

          &lt;div class=&#34;form-group&#34;&gt;
            &lt;label for=&#34;hl-pre&#34;&gt;Precondition P&lt;/label&gt;
            &lt;input type=&#34;text&#34; id=&#34;hl-pre&#34; class=&#34;mono-input&#34; spellcheck=&#34;false&#34; autocomplete=&#34;off&#34;&gt;
          &lt;/div&gt;
          &lt;div class=&#34;form-group&#34; id=&#34;hl-inv-group&#34;&gt;
            &lt;label for=&#34;hl-inv&#34;&gt;Loop invariant I&lt;/label&gt;
            &lt;input type=&#34;text&#34; id=&#34;hl-inv&#34; class=&#34;mono-input&#34; spellcheck=&#34;false&#34; autocomplete=&#34;off&#34;&gt;
          &lt;/div&gt;
          &lt;div class=&#34;form-group&#34;&gt;
            &lt;label for=&#34;hl-post&#34;&gt;Postcondition Q&lt;/label&gt;
            &lt;input type=&#34;text&#34; id=&#34;hl-post&#34; class=&#34;mono-input&#34; spellcheck=&#34;false&#34; autocomplete=&#34;off&#34;&gt;
          &lt;/div&gt;
          &lt;div id=&#34;hl-error&#34; class=&#34;error-text&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

          &lt;div class=&#34;control-buttons&#34;&gt;
            &lt;button type=&#34;button&#34; class=&#34;btn btn-primary&#34; id=&#34;btn-hl-check&#34;&gt;Check VCs&lt;/button&gt;
            &lt;button type=&#34;button&#34; class=&#34;btn btn-secondary&#34; id=&#34;btn-hl-step&#34;&gt;Step&lt;/button&gt;
            &lt;button type=&#34;button&#34; class=&#34;btn btn-danger btn-wide&#34; id=&#34;btn-hl-reset&#34;&gt;Reset&lt;/button&gt;
          &lt;/div&gt;

          &lt;div class=&#34;console-panel&#34;&gt;
            &lt;h4 class=&#34;sub-panel-title&#34;&gt;Weakest precondition trace&lt;/h4&gt;
            &lt;div id=&#34;hl-logs&#34; class=&#34;console-log tall&#34; aria-live=&#34;polite&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
          &lt;/div&gt;
        &lt;/div&gt;

        &lt;div class=&#34;fv-visual-panel&#34;&gt;
          &lt;div class=&#34;panel-header-toolbar&#34;&gt;
            &lt;span class=&#34;panel-subtitle&#34;&gt;Annotated program and verification conditions&lt;/span&gt;
            &lt;span id=&#34;hl-status&#34; class=&#34;badge badge-neutral&#34;&gt;IDLE&lt;/span&gt;
          &lt;/div&gt;

          &lt;div class=&#34;code-verification-grid&#34;&gt;
            &lt;div class=&#34;code-editor-mock&#34;&gt;
              &lt;h4 class=&#34;sub-panel-title&#34;&gt;Program&lt;/h4&gt;
              &lt;div id=&#34;hl-code-display&#34; class=&#34;code-lines-box&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
            &lt;/div&gt;

            &lt;div class=&#34;vc-proof-panel&#34;&gt;
              &lt;h4 class=&#34;sub-panel-title&#34;&gt;Verification conditions&lt;/h4&gt;
              &lt;div id=&#34;hl-vc-list&#34; class=&#34;vc-list-box&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
            &lt;/div&gt;
          &lt;/div&gt;

          &lt;p class=&#34;hint-text&#34;&gt;VCs are checked by trying every integer combination in a small range, so a pass is strong evidence rather than a proof. Only partial correctness is checked here, not termination.&lt;/p&gt;
        &lt;/div&gt;
      &lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;

  &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;script src=&#34;http://localhost:1313/js/fv_playground.js?v=806596df&#34;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;

&lt;h2 id=&#34;what-you-are-looking-at&#34;&gt;What you are looking at&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DPLL SAT solver.&lt;/strong&gt; A SAT solver decides whether a propositional formula has a satisfying assignment. DPLL guesses a value for one variable, follows every consequence it is forced into (unit propagation), and backtracks when a clause becomes false. The tree shows guesses as circles and forced assignments as diamonds. The pigeonhole example is worth stepping through: you cannot put three pigeons into two holes without two of them sharing, and the solver has to rule out every option before it can say so.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CTL model checker.&lt;/strong&gt; The four systems are written as small guarded-command programs. The checker builds every reachable state from them, then works out which states satisfy each part of your formula, from the inside out. Press Step to watch that happen one subformula at a time. When a property fails you get a counterexample run, and for properties like EF you get a witness. Peterson&amp;rsquo;s algorithm passes everything. Remove the turn variable and it still keeps the processes apart, but it can deadlock. The naive lock fails at the most basic job, and the checker shows you the exact interleaving that breaks it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hoare logic verifier.&lt;/strong&gt; A Hoare triple {P} S {Q} says that if P holds before program S runs, then Q holds after it. The verifier works backwards from Q, computing the weakest precondition of each statement, and turns the result into verification conditions (VCs). Loops need an invariant, which you provide. You can edit any of the conditions. Try weakening an invariant and see which VC breaks, and what counterexample it gives you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;why-this-matters&#34;&gt;Why this matters&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Testing can show that a program works on the inputs you tried. Formal verification aims to show that it works on all of them, or to find the case where it does not. That is why these ideas show up wherever failures are expensive: hardware design, operating system kernels like seL4, flight software and communication protocols. Real tools are far more capable than these toys, but the core ideas are the same.&lt;/p&gt;
</description>
