    <item>
      <title>Sentiment Analysis Using BERT</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/project/sentiment-analysis/</link>
      <pubDate>Thu, 26 Oct 2023 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/project/sentiment-analysis/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;institution&#34;&gt;Institution&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;National University of Sciences and Technology, Islamabad, Pakistan&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;em&gt;Oct 2023 - Dec 2023&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;project-description&#34;&gt;Project Description&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For this project I built a sentiment classifier using BERT (Bidirectional Encoder Representations from Transformers). BERT reads each word in the context of the whole sentence, which matters a lot for sentiment, where a single word like &amp;ldquo;not&amp;rdquo; can flip the meaning.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;project-highlights&#34;&gt;Project Highlights&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fine-tuned pre-trained BERT models for sentiment classification instead of training from scratch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepared the text data with standard NLP preprocessing before training.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Wrote the pipeline in Python using HuggingFace Transformers and TensorFlow.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;technical-skills-acquired&#34;&gt;Technical Skills Acquired&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Python&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Natural Language Processing (NLP)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BERT&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Machine Learning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data Preprocessing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</description>
